    "main_gap": "The central 'finite blocker' lemma—that a pairwise-intersecting family of finite sets has finitely many minimal finite transversals—is false (e.g. E_k={b_1,...,b_k,a_k} has minimal transversals {a_1,...,a_{i-1},b_i} for all i), and its König-style proof is bogus.",
    "notes": "Correct, standard reduction: the sequence enumerates S={x: gcd(x,a_i)>1 for all i} from a_1 on, and if S is a finite union of multiple-sets then periodicity follows. But the crux—no arithmetic input is used—rests on a false purely set-theoretic lemma, so the essential argument is missing.",
